From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ziteng Xiao <xiaox@gaymail.cn>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: allow off-channel scan while beaconing on DFS
 channel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

nl80211_trigger_scan() validates every requested scan channel: if
cfg80211_off_channel_oper_allowed() returns false, the channel must be
within the interface's operating bandwidth, otherwise the whole scan
request is rejected with -EBUSY.

cfg80211_off_channel_oper_allowed() implements the policy "we cannot
leave radar channels": when the operating channel itself is a radar
channel (DFS primary), every scan channel outside the operating
bandwidth is rejected.

On hardware which software-scans (e.g. MT7986A with the integrated
DBDC Wi-Fi 6 driven by mt7915e, which does not register .hw_scan), an
AP on a DFS primary channel (e.g. ch64 with HE160) can therefore never
scan channels outside its own 160 MHz block: "iw scan" fails with
-EBUSY, even with the mac80211 ieee80211_can_leave_ch() relaxation
already applied.

Relax the radar-link check the same way mac80211 was relaxed: beacons
pause during the off-channel window and radar detection resumes once
back on the operating channel.

Tested on Netcore N60 Pro (MT7986A): full-band scanning on ch64+HE160
previously failed with -EBUSY and now succeeds.

Fixes: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/26572
Signed-off-by: Ziteng Xiao <xiaox@gaymail.cn>
(cherry picked from commit a89e61a704a6d8082fea409f37806666cbe26802)
---
 net/wireless/nl80211.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/net/wireless/nl80211.c
+++ b/net/wireless/nl80211.c
@@ -10414,8 +10414,14 @@
 		link_radio_idx = cfg80211_get_radio_idx_by_chan(wdev->wiphy,
 								chandef->chan);
 		if (link_radio_idx == radio_idx) {
-			all_ok = false;
-			break;
+			/*
+			 * Relax: allow off-channel scan while beaconing on a DFS
+			 * channel. Beacons pause during the off-channel window and
+			 * radar detection resumes once back on the operating
+			 * channel, same rationale as the mac80211
+			 * ieee80211_can_leave_ch() relaxation.
+			 */
+			continue;
 		}
 	}

